---
import SpotifyEmbed from "@/components/SpotifyEmbed.astro"
import { buttonVariants } from "@/components/ui/button"
import VideoEmbed from "@/components/VideoEmbed.astro"
import { Wrapper } from "@/components/Wrapper"
import "@/styles/global.css"
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <!-- big thanks to Jan Antonin Kolar (https://unsplash.com/@jankolar) for the wonderfull banner image!  -->
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />

    <title>Michelle Howard</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <Wrapper client:load>
      <h1 class="mainPageTitle">Michelle Howard</h1>
      <div class="typeset typeset-article">
        <p class="pb-4">
          It has been our great pleasure to speak with Michelle Howard several
          times about many things related to living books and homeschooling. It
          was our particular privilege to work with Michelle to create a video
          that librarians, homeschoolers, and lovers of good books could watch
          and share as we all endeavor to better understand what a living book
          truly is and why it matters so much. On this page, we hope to pull
          together those resources and a few others to make it easy for
          librarians to find it all and make use of it.
        </p>
        <img src="/michelle-1.webp" />
        <h2 class="text-center">Living Books Video</h2>
        <p>
          In one of our podcast chats with Michelle, she told us about the
          essential conversation she has with all of her new patrons. Many of
          our listeners reached out begging to hear more of that talk. But it
          was obvious that what we really needed was a video so she could show
          us the books side by side.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong
            >This long video is perfect for librarians, educators, and those
            interested in a detailed comparison of non-living and living books.</strong
          >
        </p>
        <p>
          This short video is a trailer for a much more comprehensive video
          linked below. This video is perfect for sharing on social media, with
          donors, and with patrons. <a
            href="https://www.biblioguides.com/libraries/"
            target="_blank"
            >Special thanks to our friends at Biblioguides for hosting the video
            and the Private Lending Library Directory</a
          >. You can share this video link when sharing:
        </p>
        <code class="bg-transparent py-2 text-lg"
          >https://vimeo.com/936289740?share=copy</code
        >

        <VideoEmbed src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/936289740" />
        <h2>Interviews with Michelle Howard</h2>
        <p>
          In June of 2023, we had the joy of chatting with Michelle on the
          Plumfield Moms podcast for the first time. In that interview, we heard
          about the miraculous ways in which God guided her into this library
          work. Michelle told us how it all started, encouraged us to understand
          how much God cares about this work, and left us inspired and eager to
          nurture our own libraries well:
        </p>
        <SpotifyEmbed episodeId="13SUP93pRfHRDguuis2J7q" />
        <p>
          And our follow-up conversation about composing a Living Books
          Education portfolio for college applications
        </p>
        <SpotifyEmbed episodeId="6wG4rqPmmyumcAnu9sUrdZ" />
        <p>
          Michelle has a 20-Question Living Books Library series on her <a
            href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NW7S-lgU_Xk"
            >YouTube channel.</a
          >
        </p>
        <VideoEmbed
          src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/NW7S-lgU_Xk?si=L76gprbN25AlkWv7"
        />
        <p>
          You can learn more about Michelle and how she can help you at her
          website.
        </p>
        <div class="flex justify-center px-4 pt-6">
          <a
            href="https://www.livingbookslady.com"
            class={buttonVariants({ variant: "default" }) +
              "no-underline! hover:no-underline! text-lg!  md:w-3/4 w-full"}
            >Michelle's Website</a
          >
        </div>
        <h2>Private Lending Library Directory</h2>
        <p>
          Looking for a lending library near you? Check out the directory hosted
          by our friends at Biblioguides. If you have a library, register today!
          It's totally free and you control your information.
        </p>
        <div class="flex justify-center p-4">
          <a
            href="https://www.biblioguides.com/libraries/"
            class={buttonVariants({ variant: "default" }) +
              "no-underline! hover:no-underline! text-lg! md:w-3/4 w-full"}
            >Library Directory</a
          >
        </div>
        <h2>Are you wondering if this is something you could do?</h2>
        <div class="flex justify-center p-4">
          <a
            href="/ask-the-librarian/26"
            class={buttonVariants({ variant: "default" }) +
              "no-underline! hover:no-underline! text-lg!  md:w-3/4 w-full"}
            >Start Here!</a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </Wrapper>
  </body>
</html>
